---
# A deleted project whose editor shows a link's target has nothing left
# to do: that is where a walk rests, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# MEMORY.md with several writers and its readers: the person at the
# project page's editor, an agent asked to remember something, a guest
# shell through the read-write project mount, and Delete; read by the
# editor and by every turn of a project session. project_lifecycle has
# one saved bit and one writer; ui_project-page models only the editor's
# own states. project.yml's writers are the sibling flow
# project_definition_writers_yml (one flow over both files was 10738
# states).
#
# Checked against:
#   web/src/project.tsx ProjectView: the files (GET .../orb, loadFiles)
#     are read once per mount and again only after a save or a Retry;
#     the 4 s poll re-reads the detail, never the files. A failed poll
#     keeps the detail, so a deleted project's page and editor stay up.
#   web/src/orb.tsx FileEditor: the draft is the whole text; Save sends
#     it with no base version; a failed save keeps the draft and shows
#     the error; the textarea shows files[tab] when there is no draft.
#   serve/orbs.go putOrbFile: projectOr404 (a deleted project is a 404,
#     nothing is written), then projectdef.WriteFile.
#   projectdef.go WriteFile (MEMORY.md is prose: no check; atomicWrite =
#     temp + rename, which replaces a symlink instead of writing through
#     it), ReadFile (os.ReadFile: follows a symlink).
#   orb/orb.go mounts: the project dir is mounted read-WRITE at its host
#     path, so a guest shell writes MEMORY.md directly and can replace
#     it with a symlink to any host path.
#   plugins/tools canWrite: tools.write resolves symlinks before its root
#     check, so the host write tool REFUSES a MEMORY.md that links out of
#     the project (this corrects the mapped model: only reads follow it).
#   plugins/contextmd Parts: MEMORY.md is read fresh every turn
#     (os.ReadFile, following links, a missing file skipped);
#     plugins/engine parts() diffs the pieces against the frozen prompt
#     and sends a drift as a <context-update> (prompt.Reminder), a
#     removed piece as "no longer applies".
#
# State (one project "alpha", its page open with the MEMORY.md tab, one
# project session that takes turns):
#   dir     the project directory exists.
#   mem     MEMORY.md on disk: "v0" (what the page first read), "agent"
#           (v0 plus the fact an agent was asked to remember), "edit"
#           (the person's edit of v0, WITHOUT the agent's fact), "both"
#           (the person's edit of a text that had the fact), "link" (a
#           guest replaced it with a symlink to a host file), "none"
#           (deleted with the directory).
#   fm      the editor's copy (files["MEMORY.md"]) as last read: a mem
#           value, "host" for a link's target shown as MEMORY.md.
#   draft   the tab holds an unsaved draft: the copy plus the person's
#           edit, so what a save writes is a function of fm.
#   ed_err  the save error under the editor (only a deleted project's).
#   inj     the MEMORY.md the session's last turn sent the model: a mem
#           value, "host" for a link's target, "none" once it is gone.
#
# Folded: an agent's write through tools.write on the host, a guest
# heredoc, and `bough project write MEMORY.md` (relayed out of an orb or
# not) put down the same unvalidated bytes: one AgentRemembers. Every
# other path through the relay is a project.yml write (the _yml flow).
#
# Scope cuts: the person does not edit a tab showing a symlink's target
# (saving a host file's text into the project is a different gap from
# the read); nothing but the editor writes after Delete (an agent's
# MkdirAll that brings the directory back is project_delete_races); the
# panel stays up (ui_project-page closes it and drops the draft).

def view(mem):
    return "host" if mem == "link" else mem

role Project:
    action Init:
        self.dir = True
        self.mem = "v0"
        self.fm = "v0"
        self.draft = False
        self.ed_err = False
        self.inj = "v0"

    atomic action PersonEdits:
        require not self.draft and self.fm != "host"
        self.draft = True

    # PUT orb/files/MEMORY.md with the whole draft, no base version.
    # Success re-reads the files; a 404 keeps the draft beside the error.
    atomic action PersonSaves:
        require self.draft
        if self.dir:
            self.mem = "both" if self.fm in ("agent", "both") else "edit"
            self.fm = self.mem
            self.draft = False
        else:
            self.ed_err = True

    # Leaving the project and coming back remounts ProjectView: besides a
    # save, the only re-read of the files.
    atomic action ReopenPage:
        require self.dir and not self.draft and self.fm != view(self.mem)
        self.fm = view(self.mem)

    # An agent asked to remember something writes MEMORY.md.
    atomic action AgentRemembers:
        require self.dir and self.mem in ("v0", "edit")
        self.mem = "agent" if self.mem == "v0" else "both"

    # A guest shell replaces MEMORY.md with a symlink to a host path.
    atomic action GuestLinksMemory:
        require self.dir and self.mem != "link"
        self.mem = "link"

    # DELETE /api/projects/alpha from another tab (or `bough project rm`).
    atomic action DeleteProject:
        require self.dir
        self.dir = False
        self.mem = "none"

    # A turn of the project session: context-md re-reads MEMORY.md
    # (following a link) and a drift reaches the model.
    atomic action TurnStarts:
        require self.inj != view(self.mem)
        self.inj = view(self.mem)

action Init:
    project = Project()

# --- What holds.

# Nothing brings a deleted project back: a save to it is a 404.
transition assertion NoResurrection(before, after):
    return before.project.dir or not after.project.dir

always assertion DeletedHasNoMemory:
    return project.dir or project.mem == "none"

# A save to a deleted project keeps the draft and says why.
transition assertion DeletedSaveKeepsDraft(before, after):
    b = before.project
    a = after.project
    return b.dir or not b.draft or (a.draft and (a.ed_err or a.inj != b.inj))

# The host never writes through a symlinked MEMORY.md: a link ends only
# by a save renaming over it, or the delete.
transition assertion NoWriteThroughLink(before, after):
    b = before.project
    a = after.project
    return b.mem != "link" or a.mem in ("link", "edit", "both", "none")

# Every turn sends what is on disk as it starts.
transition assertion TurnSendsDisk(before, after):
    return before.project.inj == after.project.inj or after.project.inj == view(after.project.mem)

# --- What SHOULD hold and does not. Each was appended to this spec and
# fizz failed it; the counterexamples are in the commit that added the
# flow. Kept as comments so the spec models the product as it is.
#
# A save never overwrites a version the editor never displayed:
#   transition assertion NoLostUpdate(before, after):
#       b = before.project
#       a = after.project
#       return not (b.draft and not a.draft and a.dir) or view(b.mem) == b.fm
#
# Reading MEMORY.md never follows a symlink out of the project:
#   always assertion NoSymlinkRead:
#       return project.fm != "host" and project.inj != "host"
#
# A clean editor eventually shows disk, so an agent's remembered fact
# appears in it (the product has no re-read to make fair):
#   always eventually assertion CleanEditorCatchesUp:
#       p = project
#       return not p.dir or p.draft or p.fm == view(p.mem)
